{
  "comment": [
    "The destination table for exit mode: what the browser and the host do while",
    "an exit node is online and carrying this profile's traffic. Its sibling,",
    "tailnet-hosts.json, is the rule for every other time.",
    "",
    "Exit mode inverts the split tunnel. The whole point of an exit node is that",
    "everything leaves through it, so anything public is proxied, and what is",
    "refused is what would be dialled on somebody's LAN rather than the user's:",
    "loopback, link-local, and private address space. The exit node's LAN is not",
    "this browser's LAN, and neither is it the user's.",
    "",
    "Both implementations are tested against this file: allowExitHost in",
    "internal/proxy and tailtabExitModeProxies in extension/rules.js. They have to",
    "agree, and they have to flip modes on the same status field, or one side",
    "sends traffic the other refuses."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {"host": "github.com", "proxy": true, "why": "the public internet, which is what an exit node is for"},
    {"host": "www.google.com", "proxy": true, "why": "the public internet"},
    {"host": "ifconfig.me", "proxy": true, "why": "the public internet"},
    {"host": "8.8.8.8", "proxy": true, "why": "a public address"},
    {"host": "1.1.1.1", "proxy": true, "why": "a public address"},
    {"host": "2606:4700:4700::1111", "proxy": true, "why": "a public IPv6 address"},
    {"host": "wiki", "proxy": true, "why": "a MagicDNS short name still works in exit mode"},
    {"host": "server.tail1a2b3c.ts.net", "proxy": true, "why": "the tailnet is still reachable"},
    {"host": "100.64.0.1", "proxy": true, "why": "the tailnet's own range"},
    {"host": "100.80.1.7", "proxy": true, "why": "a tailnet address"},
    {"host": "fd7a:115c:a1e0::1", "proxy": true, "why": "the tailnet's ULA"},
    {"host": "my-tailnet.example.com", "proxy": true, "why": "a public name, whatever the suffix is"},
    {"host": "", "proxy": false, "why": "no host"},
    {"host": "localhost", "proxy": false, "why": "loopback is this machine, never the exit node's"},
    {"host": "dev.localhost", "proxy": false, "why": "loopback"},
    {"host": "127.0.0.1", "proxy": false, "why": "loopback"},
    {"host": "127.5.5.5", "proxy": false, "why": "loopback"},
